    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="1091" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/6–854: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-08T13:00:00+01:00">June 8, 1954—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 398. Repeated information London 254, Paris 397, Bangkok 18, Usun 12.
                    Reference Tosec 368.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d695-f1"/> Eden is not returning until
                    just prior to Indochina plenary this afternoon, and Bidault is leaving for Paris
                    immediately following the plenary. I believe I can obtain Bidault’s agreement
                    instruct Hoppenot to agree to language which will not specifically restrict POC
                    operations to Thailand, and will make attempt do so before Bidault’s departure
                    today. However, in view of Eden’s and Bidault’s schedules, there will be no
                    opportunity work out and agree on specific language prior to Friday.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d695-f2"/></p>
                <p>As I have previously said, I see grave dangers in negotiating this subject here
                    and had hoped that further negotiations and drafting could be centered in New
                    York and Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
